# Changelog

## 2026-11-27 — anki-tools: top-2000 nouns live, ordered new queue, gender-aware audio flags

- 1,514 new Mutable notes went live (the top-2000 noun batch plus 35 nouns for days, months, food, household items and kids' things, and 4 colour adjectives), with 2,996 recordings checked for gaps and confirmed on AnkiWeb.
- New-card order (`anki-new-due`, 10 cards a day from 2026-12-07): days, months, colours, household and kids' things, food, then the new nouns closest to English (Degrees 0–1) by frequency. Words already studied keep their schedule.
- `anki-flagged-audio --fix` redoes only the flagged gender: pink = female slots, blue = male slots, any other colour = both. It never was gender-aware before.
- вместо is voiced from the spelling вме́ста, so its unstressed final о reduces.
- A homograph's headword can carry both stresses (`за́мок / замо́к`); identity, audio and flag lookup still use the plain word.
- `anki_sync_and_restore.rebuild(path, keep_live_notetypes=True)` imports notes without touching live note types; see the runbook.
- Numeral cards show their Genitive row again (pronoun case fields no longer hide it).
- English and cue edits made on the live cards were copied into the source before the import, so it overwrote none of them.

## 2026-11-05 — anki-tools: `anki-rebalance-due` --min/--max are hard bounds

- `--min` and `--max` now hold on every day of the window in every mode (flat and `--sliding`); the exempt trailing-days tail is removed.
- Unmet bounds fail with `min unmet` / `max unmet` and write nothing; the backup is still taken first.
- With `--set-earlier`, the min pass borrows surplus from earlier days.
- Day 0 = today: `--range` accepts `0-N` and the window start (`--start-offset`) now defaults to 0. Overdue cards are still excluded.
- Runs without `--range` span to the last card, so `--min` without `--set-earlier` will often fail.
- Sliding mode: the ramp pass never drains a day below `--min`.
